--- reading it --------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. T029's core holds. A bundle fetched over the static address, installed from /data, written to
   the other slot in about 8 s, BOOT_ORDER becomes "B A" with both counters at 3, the next boot
   takes slot B (root=/dev/mmcblk0p3), the running system is the new version (VERSION=40a54ec,
   the bundle's) and health confirms it. SC-001's "one command plus one reboot" is met.
2. T028 FAILS as the image stood. Install 2 ran while slot B was pending and was not refused:
   RAUC marked B bad, rewrote it, and marked it active again. FR-009 asks for a refusal that
   names the pending state. The target of a second install is the slot that the next reboot
   will select, so this is not harmless in general, only here because the content was identical.
   RAUC only refuses to write the slot that is running. Fixed with a pre-install handler
   (T048), which needs the fixed image on the device before it can be shown.
3. The clock: the RTC was already running (a warm reboot keeps it counting from 2000-01-01), and
   ota-clock still raised it to the build time of the slot that booted. Slot B's build time is
   later than slot A's, so an update also moves the floor forward.
4. Not in this capture, still needed for T029: `rauc status` and `fw_printenv` after the reboot
   (B booted and good, A still holding the previous version, BOOT_B_LEFT back at 3) and
   `cat /data/keep` (the marker, SC-006).
5. Boot time, coarse (one-second host timestamps): SPL banner 16:08:49 to the login prompt
   16:09:00 is about 11 s, against the budget of 12.65 s. T043 must still measure it with
   grabserial.
6. Two things seen at the reboot that this feature did not cause and did not fix:
   "umount: devtmpfs busy - remounted read-only", and a new "PM: Cannot get wkup_m3_ipc handle"
   about 6.4 s in, a few lines before the wkup_m3 firmware boots normally.
